{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "אחי יהי לך אשר לך", :translit "achi yehi lakh asher lakh", :gloss "my brother, let it be to you, what is yours"} {:he "הברכות", :translit "ha-berakhot", :gloss "the blessings"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "אחי יהי לך אשר לך", :b "הברכות"}], :frame {:text "Jacob arrived at Esau having accumulated great wealth (Genesis 30:43). Rashi on Genesis 33:11, citing Genesis Rabbah 78:10, records that Jacob pressed Esau to accept his gift precisely because he wanted to recover the blessings their father Isaac had given — blessings Jacob feared had devolved upon Esau. The Ba'al HaTurim compresses this into a gematria: Esau's very words declining the gift, 'I have much, my brother; let what you have be yours,' encode the word הברכות, hinting that the entire exchange revolves around 'the blessings.'", :sources ["Genesis 30:43" "Genesis 33:11" "Genesis Rabbah 78:10" "Rashi on Genesis 33:11"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "אחי יהי לך אשר לך", :a-value 645, :b "הברכות", :b-value 633, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:09:54.379278610Z", :model "glm-5.2"}